WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.602
Zann landed in a puddle of swampy water. "Drat," he muttered.

2
00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:08.517
His Conveyance teacher was always scolding him for this sort of thing.

3
00:00:08.518 --> 00:00:12.308
Being a Red, Zann could zap himself far—and fast.

4
00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:14.716
But his focus still needed some work.

5
00:00:14.717 --> 00:00:19.469
That didn't matter now though. He was out of the house. It was time to find Darb.

6
00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:25.072
Pursing his lips, he whistled, trying to imitate the call of a lesser swamp swift.

7
00:00:25.073 --> 00:00:29.163
"Not bad," a voice said from the grassy hillock behind him.

8
00:00:29.164 --> 00:00:31.848
"I always knew you had talents other than magic."

9
00:00:31.849 --> 00:00:36.786
Zann spun around and grinned. "Hey, Darb," he said, stepping out of the water.

10
00:00:36.787 --> 00:00:40.238
"Sorry I'm late. Boz didn't want me to go out."

11
00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:46.400
"Because of the warning about Reds disappearing?" Darb asked thoughtfully. "I've been hearing about that."

12
00:00:46.401 --> 00:00:52.139
Darb was a Void, one of a small group of people in Magica born without any magical abilities.

13
00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:55.173
That was the reason he and Zann had met in the first place.

14
00:00:55.174 --> 00:01:02.790
On Zann's first day at the Swamp Bottom School, he'd encountered Jev and his friends teasing Darb. Zann had told them to stop.

15
00:01:02.791 --> 00:01:05.977
"Who's going to make me?" Jev had sneered.

16
00:01:05.978 --> 00:01:09.809
"That red hair of yours doesn't mean you get to tell me what to do."

17
00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.303
Then he'd turned and shoved Darb into the wall—hard.

18
00:01:13.304 --> 00:01:17.270
Looking back, Zann knew he probably should have called a teacher.

19
00:01:17.271 --> 00:01:23.027
Instead he'd acted on impulse, rubbing his fingers together until sparks began to jump from his hand. Jev

20
00:01:23.028 --> 00:01:28.260
didn’t even know what had happened until his friends started snickering and pointing at him. Zann

21
00:01:28.261 --> 00:01:31.726
had given him a pair of oversized donkey ears. It

22
00:01:31.727 --> 00:01:34.662
took Jev several tries to undo the spell. Ever

23
00:01:34.663 --> 00:01:39.670
since then Jev had been Zann's enemy, and Darb had been Zann's friend. Darb

24
00:01:39.671 --> 00:01:45.896
didn't attend school anymore. Voids were only required to study the basics of theory and history. Once

25
00:01:45.897 --> 00:01:51.944
classes started doing practical magic lessons, Voids usually dropped out and studied on their own. Most

26
00:01:51.945 --> 00:02:00.505
ended up finding careers as companions, greeters, animal caretakers, and mediators, or other jobs that required no magic. Most

27
00:02:00.506 --> 00:02:05.024
people in Magica would never purposely discriminate against a Void. But

28
00:02:05.025 --> 00:02:09.801
Zann had noticed that people said things in front of Darb that they wouldn't say in front of others. It

29
00:02:09.802 --> 00:02:14.290
was as if they thought Voids were deaf and dumb as well as lacking magic. That

30
00:02:14.291 --> 00:02:19.238
didn't seem fair to Zann. But it did allow Darb to hear a lot of interesting gossip. "What

31
00:02:19.239 --> 00:02:22.878
have you heard about the warning?" Zann asked his friend now. "Not

32
00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:27.768
much," Darb said. "Everyone's talking about the message from the palace though. The

33
00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:33.017
mayor is so nervous that she put a Shield spell over the entire town hall." "Boz

34
00:02:33.018 --> 00:02:35.374
is trying to find out more. In

35
00:02:35.375 --> 00:02:40.549
the meantime he wants me to stay inside." Zann rolled his eyes. "You

36
00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:44.380
can't blame him for being worried after what happened to your parents." "I

37
00:02:44.381 --> 00:02:49.816
guess." Zann jumped onto a larger hillock. "So what have you been doing?" "Studying

38
00:02:49.817 --> 00:02:51.638
insects." "Insects,

39
00:02:51.639 --> 00:02:58.064
huh?" Zann said. "Why not study something more exciting? Dragons, maybe?" "Speaking

40
00:02:58.065 --> 00:03:01.983
of dragons, where's Zing?" Darb asked. "He

41
00:03:01.984 --> 00:03:06.400
was outside when I left. I couldn't get him without Boz seeing me." Darb

42
00:03:06.401 --> 00:03:11.625
looked disappointed. Everyone assumed he'd end up being an animal caretaker someday. He

43
00:03:11.626 --> 00:03:14.480
loved animals of all kinds, and they loved him. Zing

44
00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:18.245
broke into a happy whistling song whenever he saw him. Darb

45
00:03:18.246 --> 00:03:22.603
stepped toward a slow-moving stream. "Look, panic bugs." He

46
00:03:22.604 --> 00:03:26.937
leaned closer for a better look. "Can you get a picture of them for me?" "Sure."

47
00:03:26.938 --> 00:03:31.473
Zann rubbed his hands together and stared at the shiny red bugs. Blink

48
00:03:31.474 --> 00:03:32.476
!

49
00:03:32.477 --> 00:03:35.686
A piece of paper appeared and fluttered to the swampy ground.

50
00:03:35.687 --> 00:03:40.319
Zann picked it up. The image of the panic bugs was there in full color.

51
00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.145
"Thanks." Darb took the blink image, folded it, and put it into his pocket.

52
00:03:45.146 --> 00:03:52.366
Then he gently scooped up the bugs and put them in his other pocket, being careful not to startle them into releasing their stink.

53
00:03:52.367 --> 00:03:57.072
"Want to help me look for leeches?" he asked. "I've seen them around here before."

54
00:03:57.073 --> 00:04:00.499
"Leeches?" Zann echoed. "Why?"

55
00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:05.694
"I've been reading about them. It's fascinating how they can suck the magic out of people."

56
00:04:05.695 --> 00:04:12.986
"Yeah." Zann grinned. "Back in First City, my friends and I used to stick them on each other as a joke. It

57
00:04:12.987 --> 00:04:18.994
would take about a million of them to drain enough magic to make a difference, but it was still funny." Darb

58
00:04:18.995 --> 00:04:24.568
peered into the water's murky depths. "Leeches are very shy," he said. "They

59
00:04:24.569 --> 00:04:26.824
live at the bottom of streams like this. We'll

60
00:04:26.825 --> 00:04:29.748
have to be quiet and feel around in the water." "Why

61
00:04:29.749 --> 00:04:33.691
go to all that trouble?" Zann rubbed his fingers together. "I'll

62
00:04:33.692 --> 00:04:38.608
displace the water. Then you can grab as many leeches as you want." "Zann,

63
00:04:38.609 --> 00:04:41.763
wait!" Darb began. "That won't—" Shloop

64
00:04:41.764 --> 00:04:43.001
!

65
00:04:43.002 --> 00:04:47.961
The water in the nearest section of the stream levitated, hanging as droplets in the air.

66
00:04:47.962 --> 00:04:53.351
Several fish and other creatures were left lying on the bottom of the streambed, looking confused.

67
00:04:53.352 --> 00:05:03.592
"Leeches!" Zann cried, pointing. Almost before he spotted them, the slimy little creatures had burrowed into the soft sand. "Oh. They're gone."

68
00:05:03.593 --> 00:05:07.486
"I tried to tell you that," Darb said with a sigh.

69
00:05:07.487 --> 00:05:10.966
"They dive away from air unless they're latched on to someone."

70
00:05:10.967 --> 00:05:15.711
"Sorry," Zann said. "Hey, did you hear that?"

71
00:05:15.712 --> 00:05:17.034
"Hear what?"

72
00:05:17.035 --> 00:05:21.667
Zann tilted his head, listening. "That buzzing noise," he said.

73
00:05:21.668 --> 00:05:26.883
"Sounds like an irritated spy fly, or maybe—"

74
00:05:26.884 --> 00:05:30.505
A loud, angry buzzing drowned out his words.

75
00:05:30.506 --> 00:05:39.502
Suddenly a whole swarm of tiny, glittering dragons came zipping out of a hole in the bank and started stinging him!

